{"id":"9bb39b9d-ce4d-4a38-8aa2-d46cbbde0517","object":"chat.completion","created":1784276614,"model":"deepseek-v4-pro","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call_00_RH0tu8dAYQZC7bBAgcgb7374","type":"function","function":{"name":"Summary","arguments":"{\"summary\": \"Amazon Alexa is a virtual assistant technology developed by Amazon, launched in November 2014 alongside the Echo smart speaker. It was built on technology from two acquisitions: Evi (a British question-to-answer system founded by William Tunstall-Pedoe, acquired 2012) and Ivona (a Polish speech synthesizer, acquired 2013).\\n\\nAlexa is available across multiple platforms including Fire OS, iOS, Android, Linux, Windows, and Wear OS, supporting languages such as English, French, German, Japanese, Italian, Spanish, Portuguese, Hindi, and Arabic. It performs tasks including voice interaction, music playback, setting alarms, streaming podcasts, providing weather/traffic/sports updates, and controlling smart home devices. Users activate Alexa via a wake word (default \\\"Alexa\\\") or button press on certain devices.\\n\\nA key feature is the Alexa Skills Kit, allowing third-party developers to build \\\"skills\\\" (apps). As of April 2019, there were over 90,000 skills available, up from 1,000 in June 2016. By January 2019, Amazon had sold over 100 million Alexa-enabled devices.\\n\\nDespite widespread adoption, Alexa struggled to generate expected revenue from voice ordering. By 2022, the division was losing several billion dollars per quarter, leading to mass layoffs. In response, Amazon shifted toward generative AI: in November 2023, employees were directed to train a large language model codenamed \\\"Olympus,\\\" and in December 2024, Amazon announced its Nova brand of AI models. In February 2025, Amazon introduced Alexa+, a generative AI-powered version free for Prime members, with Anthropic's Claude models integrated. In January 2026, Alexa+ expanded to the web via Alexa.com, competing directly with ChatGPT and Gemini. Alexa+ became available to all U.S. users on February 4, 2026. In early 2026, Amazon entered discussions to invest up to $50 billion in OpenAI.\\n\\nAdditional features include home automation (compatible with devices from Philips Hue, Nest, Ring, etc.), food ordering from services like Domino's and Grubhub, sports updates for 15 leagues, messaging and calling, Alexa for Business, severe weather alerts, and traffic updates. The Alexa Voice Service (AVS) allows manufacturers to integrate Alexa into their products at no cost.\", \"key_excerpts\": \"As of November 2018, more than 10,000 Amazon employees worked on Alexa and related products. In January 2019, Amazon's devices team announced that they had sold over 100 million Alexa-enabled devices., Amazon developers chose the name Alexa because it has a hard consonant with the X, which helps it be recognized with higher precision. They have said the name is reminiscent of the Library of Alexandria., In 2022, with the division losing several billion dollars per quarter, the company started laying off Alexa employees en masse., In February 2025, Amazon introduced Alexa+, the latest version of their voice assistant, which is powered by generative AI. Alexa+ was announced to be free for all Prime members., In early 2026, Amazon entered advanced discussions to invest up to $50 billion in OpenAI as part of a potential artificial intelligence partnership so that OpenAI's models could be integrated into Amazon's digital assistant Alexa and other internal projects.\"}"}}]},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"tool_calls"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":5509,"completion_tokens":724,"total_tokens":6233,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":5504},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":5504,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":5},"system_fingerprint":"fp_9954b31ca7_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}